00:04:46.199 --> 00:04:49.389
It is outlined in the 10th Amendment.

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:54.800
And the 10th Amendment lays out the default
power dynamics between state and federal government,

00:04:54.800 --> 00:05:00.800
where it says, quote, The powers not delegated
to the United States by the Constitution nor

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:07.650
prohibited by it to the states are reserved
to the states, respectively, or to the people.

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:13.849
So, in other words, if there is some action
or power that the Constitution or Bill of

00:05:13.849 --> 00:05:21.389
Rights don't specifically say the federal
government has power over this and the Constitution

00:05:21.389 --> 00:05:25.699
